p=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent; sha=lambda b:hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest(); r=json.loads((p/'reservation.json').read_text()); prov=json.loads((p/'provenance.json').read_text()); inv=json.loads((p/'passage-inventory.json').read_text())
data={
321501:('excluded_published_counterexample','Stolee original regularity motivation; Hartke–Stolee Construction 23 and Figure 19, PDF pages 34 and 37. Figure visually read.','The published 16-vertex 5-primitive graph has degrees 8 at v1,v2 and 9 at the fourteen other vertices, hence no degree-15 dominating vertex and is irregular. Its printed uniquely K5-saturated property directly refutes the universal regularity claim.','No new mechanism: rechecking this exact printed graph would be a known-result formalization. Full unique-completion verification was not independently executed.'),
321554:('parked_correction_and_spectral_gap','Definition 1, Conjecture 1 and adjacent trace-kernel proof in v1,v2,v3. A 2025 corrigendum was located; publisher HTTP 403.','The trace-kernel complement works when the eigenvalue is in the field and n is invertible: subtract tr(M)/n times I. This does not address absent field eigenvalues or characteristic dividing n.','Need a linear scalar-eigenvalue functional in the full 1-spec convention, including inseparable cases. The corrigendum concerns algebraic-closure spectra and n=4 and does not by itself settle n>4 here. No classification or full source clearance.'),
321621:('excluded_published_counterexample','Kim–Koberda Conjecture 4 in all three versions; Casals-Ruiz–Duncan–Kazachkov arXiv:1306.3087 Section 3, Lemma 3.1 proof and portions of Lemma 3.2.','The printed five-generator group embeds into the printed six-generator group via a -> a1 a2 and identity on b,c,d,e; Lemma 3.2 rules out induced inclusion into the extension graph. This is the exact failed implication.','Published refutation. Lemma 3.2 full case analysis and journal/version history of the counterexample paper were not completely audited; this limits review depth, not grounds to claim novelty.'),
321728:('parked_sustained_latin_rectangle_route','All three target passages; latest Lemma 2, Theorem 3 proof for complete-by-complete products and Section 4 boundary discussion.','See ORDINARY-ATTEMPTS.md: a cyclic Latin rectangle reduces to injectivity of ordered-pair colors 2a_r-a_s. At q=m(m-1) every full color must be distinct and use every available color; source greedy extension loses its last slack.','Need a uniform construction of the tight Latin rectangles, or an admissible n with a proof of nonexistence. A finite parameter check would not prove the all-n claim, and no obstructing n is supplied.'),
321938:('excluded_published_full_proof','All three source PDFs retrieved; latest Conjecture 1.6 and sharp example; journal version; Matomaki On sumsets of multisets in Z_p^m, Theorem 5 and full Section 3 proof read.','Matomaki Conjecture 4 is exactly the bound for size p+k, k<=p-3, plus an extra endpoint. Theorem 5 proves it for every k, using saturation of one-dimensional fibers, induction, and extension to size 2p-2. Therefore it directly includes the literal assigned statement.','Zero discovery credit. Auxiliary Lemmas 13–16 and publication chronology not completely independently audited; no new witness or alternative proof pursued.'),
322014:('parked_existential_frame_gap','Latest Definition 2.3 and Example 2.5, Definition 5.2, Conjectures 13.8–13.9; early-version geometric definitions; historical r272 result 322013.','A cone vertex must lie in every maximal face of each relevant fiber. Strong stratification additionally requires every intersection flat to carry a face of the prescribed dimension. Real Coxeter and Shephard constructions are already supplied by the source.','Need rank-sized generating reflections AND a frame for all remaining well-generated groups. A bad choice of frame does not refute the existential statement. Earlier-version target locations and journal/citing bodies not fully reviewed.'),
322024:('parked_minimal_transversal_gap','v3/v4 Conjecture 9.6 and following explanation, including B3 k=2 compatibility warning. v1/v2 retrieved, target passage not located by text screen.','A nonface is a set of positions meeting every reduced w0 subword of Q=c^k w0(c). Minimal nonfaces are minimal transversals; the source proves size >=k+1 and supplies A,B,dihedral cases.','Need to prove every such minimal transversal has size <=k+1 outside known types, or give a larger minimal transversal with all proper subsets verified. Pairwise incompatibility fails already in the printed B3 example; no new witness.'),
322081:('parked_uniform_finite_field_classification','Both versions Conjecture 1; source conclusion and named three families. A 2022 primary problem list identifies the even-n case as solved by Gologlu.','Normalizing a nonzero derivative increment reduces APN to fibers of D_t(X)=(X+1)^(2^t-1)+X^(2^t-1). A refutation needs an additional exponent whose every derivative fiber has size <=2, not one collision-free sample.','No new exponent or uniform odd-n exclusion. Even-n result is known; Gologlu proof body and all later APN classification bodies remain unread.'),
322155:('excluded_printed_counterexample','Latest Conjecture 1.1 and counterexample paragraph; Figure 1 on PDF page 2 visually inspected. Earlier versions fetched, target passages not fully compared.','The cited paper itself prints a critical girth-four graph with nine vertices and thirteen edges, average degree 26/9<3, without C3 or K2,3 subgraphs. This directly refutes the exact general conjecture.','The authors leave non-labelability and proper-subgraph labelability as exercises; those were not independently proved here. Reusing their figure or expanding its exercise is a known-outcome formalization.'),
322271:('parked_cycle_spectrum_gap','Latest Conjecture 8 and surrounding reduction through cubic claw-free triangle expansion; earlier versions retrieved but only partial passages read.','Admissible integer cycle lengths lie in the union of intervals (2^k/3,2^(k-1)]. Triangle expansion yields lengths 2l through 3l. Selecting a shortest cycle alone does not force an admissible interval.','Need a uniform cycle-spectrum lemma for every cubic graph, or an actual cubic graph whose full cycle spectrum avoids every interval. Neither a witness nor a sound small exhaustive bound is supplied.'),
322351:('parked_serial_exchange_gap','All three Conjecture 1.4 passages; introduction and rank-four result routing.','Distance from any base to its complement is at least n because each edge replaces one element. Symmetric exchange gives neighbors, but not a path that gains one prescribed target element at every step.','Need connectivity and a sharp n-step path between arbitrary base-cobases. Restricting to graphic, transversal, sparse paving or small rank is not the exact all-matroid claim. No credible full route.'),
322389:('parked_likely_known_modern_theorem_scope_unchecked','Source Conjecture 1.2 and surrounding dichotomy read; modern Hadari/Liu homological-eigenvalue results located through search only.','A finite characteristic refinement and transfer can preserve an eigenvalue >1; making EVERY lift work also needs deck/power compatibility. Presence of a pseudo-Anosov component is the relevant modern theorem hypothesis.','Modern theorem bodies and reducible/subsurface/all-lifts scope not audited; do not turn a search lead into a proved reduction. Park for known-outcome reconciliation, no new route.'),
322520:('parked_modern_cluster_uniqueness_scope_unchecked','All four versions rigidity target passages; latest frozen-row-preserving equivalence definition and Conjectures 3.11–3.12.','Equivalent extended matrices determine c-vector data up to mutable-column permutation with frozen rows fixed. A c-vector uniqueness theorem would identify the seed; principal-part periodicity alone does not suffice.','Need actual current sign-coherence/tropical-duality/seed-uniqueness theorem bodies in full skew-symmetrizable scope and their exact implication. No new rank-two example or known-family variant claimed.'),
322711:('parked_simultaneous_weight_gap','All three Conjecture 9 passages; latest Proposition 8 proof and printed multiplicity recipe.','For one target edge the source puts multiplicities p^2 on a crossing pair and p^4 on the rest of a Kuratowski subgraph. Two separate applications need not preserve the first edge criticality: their optimal drawings can differ.','Need a common weighting forcing both edges essential in crossing-number minimization, or a graph with proof that every integer weighting fails. No simultaneous construction established.'),
322716:('parked_sustained_partition_route','All three Conjecture 5.1 passages; v1 allows 1<x<=y+z whereas v2/v3 impose y<x. Latest Theorem 4.1 proof and Theorem 4.2 comparison read. Publisher 403.','See ORDINARY-ATTEMPTS.md: product inequality gives strictly positive dominant coefficient at q=1; all other roots of unity have lower pole order, proving eventual positivity for each fixed tuple. The source already handles z=2, odd y, m=2y+2.','Missing nonnegativity of EVERY coefficient for z not dividing y. A direct residue injection lacks recoverability of original multiplicities. The eventual result is only a partial classical bridge and is not a full solution or Pi-qualified certificate.'),
324363:('parked_global_metric_gap','Latest Conjecture 5.24, surrounding three/four-point values and universal n/(2n-2) bound. Earlier 1101.0106 companion not fetched.','Regular triangle attains sqrt(3)/2; the global lower bound must compare every finite planar metric minimal filling with its Steiner minimal tree. The generic bound n/(2n-2) tends to 1/2 and cannot imply sqrt(3)/2.','No uniform geometric inequality or strict counterexample. Do not substitute the distinct classical Steiner ratio claim. Companion/version/journal coverage remains incomplete.'),
324369:('excluded_source_theorem','Source Theorem 2.2 and full proof, Lemma 2.1 full proof, Corollary 2.3 read in latest single arXiv version.','Theorem 2.2 has exactly finite simple connected bipartite n>=4,m>=n hypotheses and conclusion Sz-W>=4n-8. It decomposes into blocks after proving the two-connected case via pair contributions. Equality example also matches literally.','The source itself solves the assigned conjecture. Independent repair or formalization would not be a new outcome. Separate 1104.2122 companion and final journal body not fully read.'),
325182:('parked_sustained_monoid_normal_form_route','Single arXiv version and journal Conjecture 5.1; Section 5 definition, parabolic separation, [4321]/[4231] discussion.','Without mu_N, paired generators split into commuting halves and the source describes a double-Catalan quotient. With mu_N present, middle-boundary crossings couple the halves, so the parabolic fiber theorem cannot count the full monoid.','Need a unique normal form or explicit bijection to triples (two j-subsets of [N], a Catalan object of size j), including reachability and uniqueness. No normal form handles arbitrarily many middle-generator returns. Thesis 1108.4379 remains unread.'),
340762:('parked_infinite_topological_gap','Both versions Conjecture 2 and Fig.6 discussion; finite local-Hamiltonicity theorem routing.','Finite compatible cycles must survive an exhaustion and form a topological circle through every vertex and end. A limit of cycles can split into a disconnected spanning 2-regular object or meet an end incorrectly.','Need end-faithful connected limiting-cycle construction under the exact degree and radius-two hypotheses. A finite witness cannot by itself refute this infinite statement. Earlier three source families remain unread.'),
352341:('parked_global_optimality_gap','Both versions Conjecture 1 and adjacent statements that n=6 is known; Mossinghoff family context.','Symmetric stationary polygons give lower bounds. A counterexample to the conjecture needs a globally optimal asymmetric polygon or an asymmetric feasible polygon exceeding a proved upper bound for every symmetric polygon.','No global extremal certificate. Source diameter-graph theorem does not force axial symmetry. Earlier 1103.4456 and all optimizer proof bodies not read.')}
